  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Criminal Behavior Associations",
  "description": "The meme relies on the harmful stereotype that Black people are inherently criminal or associated with incarceration, which is used to mock the 'Black Lives Matter' movement by implying that if Black lives are 'in prison', then they don't matter. This stereotype is a real-world concept used to delegitimize Black communities and is central to understanding the meme's hateful intent.",
